0. Purpose, Scope & Traceability
This handoff translates the MICROFI System Architecture and Software Design (SAD v1.1) into concrete screen-
level UI specifications for three surfaces: the Flutter Agent app, the Flutter Client app, and the Next.js 16 Back-
Office. Every screen in this document is traceable to a use case (UC), functional requirement (FR), non-functional
requirement (NFR) or business rule (BR) defined in the SAD and its upstream Business Analysis.
This document supersedes v1.1 of the UI/UX handoff. Notable corrections driven by the SAD: the client digital
booklet token has four states (ACTIVE / GRACE / EXPIRED / REVOKED), not two; collection screens must reflect
the mandatory GPS gate as a hard block (BR-05); tracking and session UI must respect branch working-hours
windows (FR-15, NFR-10); and OFJ close must remain blocked while any collection is still sync_status =
PENDING.
See the Glossary (final section) for definitions of all acronyms and domain terms used throughout this document.
