4. Agent Mobile App (Flutter) — Collection Zone
4.1 Authentication (UC-01)
• Launch screen reads device IMEI silently in the background, then prompts PIN or biometric.
• Unknown/unbound IMEI: full-screen red block — "This device is not registered to an agent account. Contact
your branch manager." No retry loop offered on-device.
• 3 failed PIN attempts locks the session for a cooldown period; a countdown is shown.
• Offline authentication is supported against the encrypted local credential cache when no network is present.
4.2 Session Window & Working Hours (UC-15, FR-15, NFR-10)
• Outside the branch's configured open/close window, the app shows a locked dashboard state: "Collections are
closed until [open_time]" with no wizard entry point.
• GPS background tracking (UC-10) automatically stops outside the working window, per NFR-10; the
connectivity/tracking icon in the header reflects this as a neutral grey "Tracking paused" chip rather than the
amber offline state.
4.3 "Fat-Finger" Accessibility Baseline
• Minimum action button height: 48 dp, for use in open-air markets with hands often full or gloved.
• Persistent top connectivity banner: hidden when online; amber "Offline Mode — [X] collections ready to
sync" when offline; grey "Tracking paused" outside working hours.
4.4 Escrow Wallet & Ceiling (UC-03, UC-04, UC-05)
• Home dashboard shows a compact gauge for escrow_account.balance_xaf against ceiling_xaf, colored per the
thresholds in Section 1.1.
• At 100% of ceiling, new collections are blocked at the client-lookup step with a red banner and lock icon,
before the agent invests time entering client/denomination data.
• Remote ceiling overrides (UC-05, pushed from Back-Office) apply live without requiring an app restart, and
display a countdown to valid_until.
4.5 Three-Step Collection Wizard (UC-06, UC-07, UC-08, UC-12)
[ Step 1: Client ] ──(resolved)──> [ Step 2: Denominations ] ──(GPS gate)──> [ Step 3: Confirmation ]
Step 1 — Client Resolution (UC-06)
• Search field supports QR scan, member ID, phone, or name; multiple matches present a disambiguation list
rather than auto-selecting.
• On unique match: display client_profile card (name, member number, photo, branch). "Next" activates only
once exactly one client is locked.
Step 2 — Denomination Breakdown (UC-08, BR-02)
• CEMAC Grid: one row per BEAC denomination (10000 / 5000 / 2000 / 1000 / 500 XAF) plus a coins-total
field, integer-only quantities.
• Live running total = Σ(denomination × quantity); "Next" is disabled until this total equals the amount the agent
intends to collect (BR-02).
Page 7MICROFI — UI/UX Design Handoff v2.0 (SAD-aligned)
Step 3 — GPS Gate & Submission (UC-12, BR-05)
• On "Validate collection": query location services.
◦ GPS active with valid fix: discreet loader, collection saved with lat/lon/accuracy/timestamp captured
immutably (non-editable by the agent, FR-12).
◦ GPS inactive or no fix: hard-blocking red pop-up — "Action impossible. GPS must be enabled to
validate a collection." Submit stays disabled; this is a strict block, not a warning, per BR-05.
• Successful submission triggers UC-09 notification (SMS + optional Bluetooth print) and writes core.collection
with sync_status = PENDING until synced.
4.6 Field Tracking & Emergency (UC-10, UC-11, UC-13, UC-14)
• Background GPS pings (~5 min cadence) are invisible to the agent except for the header tracking indicator;
battery impact is minimized per NFR-09 (no dedicated screen).
• Geofence breach: agent-facing app does not need to surface the breach itself (this is a Back-Office concern)
but should not alarm the agent — no pop-up interrupts their workflow.
• SOS (UC-14): accessible via the side menu or a 3-second long-press on the app header. Triggers a single-pulse
vibration and a discreet confirmation message; attempts SMS delivery even with no data connectivity. Cannot
be disabled by the agent (FR-14).
5. Client Mobile App (Digital Booklet)
5.1 Activation & Renewal (UC-19)
Activation is a three-party, in-person flow between the client and their sponsoring agent — the client never enters
the temporary Activation ID directly on their own device.
• Step 1 — Client initiates: the client tells the agent they want to activate (or renew) their digital booklet.
• Step 2 — Client shares credentials with the agent: the client provides their temporary Activation ID
(activation_id) and identity details to the agent in person.
• Step 3 — Agent enters & validates: the agent enters the Activation ID and client details into their app; the app
validates the ID against CBS before proceeding.
• Step 4 — Client confirms payment: the activation fee is presented to the client, who confirms payment before
anything is finalized.
• Step 5 — Transaction validated: only after payment is confirmed is the activation completed — the token is
issued (or renewed) and the fee is split automatically between agent commission and MFI share
(activation_payment).
• Activation ID not found: the agent's app redirects to physical branch registration; the app never creates a CBS
customer record.
5.2 Booklet Token State Machine (UC-20/21/22 — access_token.status)
The SAD schema defines four token states, each requiring a distinct visual treatment — this corrects the two-state
model in the prior handoff draft:
• ACTIVE — full interface; all monetary actions available ("Request withdrawal", renewal not yet needed).
• GRACE — non-blocking amber banner: "Your annual token expires soon — renew with your agent to keep
full access." All actions remain enabled during grace.
Page 8MICROFI — UI/UX Design Handoff v2.0 (SAD-aligned)
• EXPIRED (read-only) — grey banner: "Annual token expired. Your data remains visible." Monetary action
buttons drop to 30% opacity (inactive); balance and history stay sharp and fully legible (BR-04 — money is
never locked by token status).
• REVOKED — full-screen block distinct from EXPIRED: "Your digital access has been revoked. Please
contact your branch." No balance or history is shown in this state, unlike EXPIRED.
5.3 Home / Balance (UC-21)
• Home screen visually echoes the traditional cardboard savings passbook (textured beige or brand-navy
background).
• Balance is shown in 32 pt bold regardless of token state (except REVOKED); falls back to last-cached balance
when the CBS is unreachable, with a small "as of [timestamp]" caption.
5.4 Contribution History / Mini-Statement (UC-22)
• Filterable, append-only list of collections tied to the client; supports an offline cached view.
• Empty state and USSD short-code equivalent are covered in Section 8.
