15. Glossary
TermDefinition
ACIDAtomicity, Consistency, Isolation, Durability — transactional guarantees used for
money-moving paths (Spring Data JPA).
AES-256Advanced Encryption Standard, 256-bit key — encrypts the offline collection
queue on the agent's device (NFR-01).
AMQPAdvanced Message Queuing Protocol — the messaging protocol used by
RabbitMQ to decouple Core Backend from CBS Middleware.
BEACBanque des États de l'Afrique Centrale — the central bank issuing CEMAC
banknotes; defines the denomination set (500–10,000 XAF).
BRBusiness Rule — a numbered rule from the Business Analysis (e.g. BR-05: GPS
is mandatory before any collection).
Back-OfficeThe Next.js 16 web application used by branch managers and administrators.
CBSCore Banking System — the bank's system of record (e.g. Amplitude, FinanSoft)
that MICROFI integrates with via the Middleware.
CEMACCommunauté Économique et Monétaire de l'Afrique Centrale — the six-country
monetary zone MICROFI operates in.
COBACCommission Bancaire de l'Afrique Centrale — the regional banking regulator
requiring transaction traceability.
Ceiling (escrow ceiling)The maximum cash an agent may hold before collections are automatically
blocked (BR-03).
DenominationA single banknote or coin face value (e.g. 1,000 XAF); collections are broken
down by denomination and quantity (FR-08).
Page 15MICROFI — UI/UX Design Handoff v2.0 (SAD-aligned)
TermDefinition
Device TX ID
(device_tx_id)A locally generated unique transaction identifier that lets a collection be traced
even if sync happens hours later.
Escrow accountThe agent's cash guarantee wallet (escrow_account.balance_xaf against
ceiling_xaf) that limits field cash exposure.
FRFunctional Requirement — a numbered requirement from the Business Analysis
(e.g. FR-12: mandatory GPS geotagging).
GeofenceA drawn geographic boundary an agent is expected to stay within; breaches raise
a geofence_alert.
GRACE (token state)A booklet-token state after ACTIVE and before EXPIRED, during which a
renewal reminder is shown but no functionality is restricted.
IMEI bindingLocking an agent's session to a single physical device's IMEI, part of
authentication security (FR-01).
JWTJSON Web Token — the signed token format used for agent, client and admin
session authentication.
MVPMinimum Viable Product — the reduced feature set targeted for the initial 6-
week production window.
NFRNon-Functional Requirement — a numbered quality attribute (e.g. NFR-09:
battery-usage optimisation for GPS tracking).
OFJOpération de Fin de Journée (End-of-Day operation) — the daily cash-
reconciliation and closeout process.
RabbitMQThe message broker that queues jobs between the Core Backend and the CBS
Middleware so mobile requests are never blocked on the CBS.
Sync status
(sync_status)The state of a collection record: PENDING (not yet sent) or SYNCED
(confirmed received by the server).
STRIDEA threat-modeling framework — Spoofing, Tampering, Repudiation,
Information disclosure, Denial of service, Elevation of privilege.
UCUse Case — a numbered behavioural specification (e.g. UC-16: OFJ
reconciliation) that this handoff's screens map to.
Variance (Δ)The difference between the physically counted cash and the digitally recorded
total at end-of-day (BR-01).
Variance debtA formal debt recorded against an agent when a cash shortage (negative
variance) is confirmed (UC-17).
XAF / FCFAThe CFA franc (BEAC), the currency used across the CEMAC zone; displayed
with a non-breaking space before the code, e.g. "45 000 XAF".
